#N canvas 20 20 1560 1440 12;
#X text 20 20 g_levels -- the Phase 1 display. Reads named values off the disp bus and draws the two input levels big on the OLED \, with a one-word status line underneath., f 58;
#X text 20 95 creation args: none. inlets: none. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 140 SOLE OWNER OF THE SCREEN. Nothing else in Cut It may send on oscOut or screenLine1-5. Phase 3 replaces the inside of this file with the g_oled arbiter -- layers \, priority \, TTL -- but the interface stays: consume disp \, own the screen., f 58;
#X obj 20 300 r disp;
#X obj 20 330 route in-l in-r boot;
#X obj 20 370 list split 1;
#X obj 250 370 list split 1;
#X obj 480 300 loadbang;
#X obj 480 330 del 300;
#X obj 480 360 metro 100;
#X obj 480 400 t b b b b b b;
#X msg 780 450 sendtyped /oled/gShowInfoBar ii 3 0;
#X msg 780 490 sendtyped /oled/gClear ii 3 1;
#X obj 780 530 f;
#X msg 780 560 sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiisi 3 4 28 24 1 R \$1;
#X obj 780 610 f;
#X msg 780 640 sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiisi 3 4 2 24 1 L \$1;
#X msg 780 720 sendtyped /oled/gPrintln iiiiis 3 4 54 8 1 \$1;
#X msg 780 760 sendtyped /oled/gFlip i 3;
#X obj 620 840 s oscOut;
#X obj 400 690 symbol cut-it-v0.2;
#X text 20 900 ALL EXPLANATION LIVES BELOW THE PATCH \, not beside it. Comments placed between the logic and the message column get cords drawn straight through them -- which is what happened the first time this file was written. tools/pd-layout-check.py catches it now., f 46;
#X text 20 1020 list split 1 drops the unit \, so a caller may send either name value or name value unit. The float lands in the cold inlet of an f and waits there to be drawn., f 46;
#X text 20 1130 Only the first five arguments of gPrintln must be ints. Everything after is concatenated with spaces \, so mixed symbols and numbers are fine -- checked in Organelle_UI/main.cpp., f 46;
#X text 540 900 THE DRAW RATE IS FIXED HERE at 10 Hz \, not set by how chatty the bus is. That is the whole job of a display arbiter \, in miniature: callers push semantics whenever they like \, the screen redraws on its own clock., f 46;
#X text 540 1020 The trigger order is the draw order \, rightmost outlet first: info bar off \, clear \, the text \, then flip. gFlip last is not optional -- nothing reaches the display without it., f 46;
#X text 540 1130 gShowInfoBar goes out on EVERY redraw \, not once at load. mother repaints the patch screen after loading a patch and restores the bar -- plan-display.md trap 4., f 46;
#X text 1060 900 The typetag must match the argument count EXACTLY or packOSC drops the message with an error you cannot see on the device. iiiiisi is five ints \, a symbol \, then the value -- verified against packOSC on the hardware., f 46;
#X text 1060 1020 R sits above L in this patch only \, to keep the cords from crossing. On the SCREEN L is the top line (y 2) and R the second (y 28)., f 46;
#X text 1060 1240 list append is not decoration: route emits a lone symbol as a SELECTOR \, not as a symbol message \, and [symbol] rejects that. list append converts it. Pd prints inlet: expected 'symbol' but got '...' if you skip it., f 46;
#X text 1060 1130 The bottom 8px line is one symbol \, holding whatever u_init last reported on disp as boot. It falls back to the version string \, so g_levels still says something sensible on its own., f 46;
#X obj 250 600 list append;
